<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title><%= projectName %></title>
    <!--
      The design system is loaded ONCE, as an external, and every
      bundle that needs it resolves through this map to the same URL.

      This is correctness, not size. A package that defines custom
      elements must exist exactly once per page: two bundles each
      inlining a copy throw `NotSupportedError: <tag> has already been
      used with this registry` on the second registration, and the
      throw aborts the rest of that bundle's registrations — so half
      the page silently stops upgrading. With one context there is one
      bundle and nothing to collide; the map is here so that carving a
      context into its own bundle stays a wiring change.

      An import map must precede the first module script, which is why
      it is above the one below.
    -->
    <script type="importmap">
      {
        "imports": {
          "<%= designSystemPkg %>": "/vendor/design-system.js"
        }
      }
    </script>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/vendor/design-system.css" />
    <script type="module" src="/src/main.ts"></script>
  </head>
  <body>
    <center-pk gutters="var(--s1)">
      <stack-pk space="var(--s2)">
        <typography-pk variant="heading-1"><%= projectName %></typography-pk>
        <<%= viewTag %>></<%= viewTag %>>
      </stack-pk>
    </center-pk>
  </body>
</html>
